<binaryimage arch="AARCH64:BE:64:v8A">
<!--
    Big-endian twin of kuna-wholeinputarg.xml: the same instruction bytes
    (AArch64 instructions stay little-endian) under AARCH64:BE:64:v8A, where
    the low piece of x0 sits at the register's offset + 4. P4 active-parameter
    trials (`p4_calls/kuna_wholeinputarg.rs`, no option). It pins the
    big-endian side of the piece check (the piece is the entry's least
    significant part) that PowerPC64 shares.

    The functions and assertions are those of the little-endian file, except
    the unsigned char veneer, whose return value big-endian AArch64 loses on
    the unpatched tree as well (a separate defect). In a big-endian register
    the struct's low half is its second field, so sfld passes s.b.

    No upstream issue. On the unpatched tree #1, #3, #4 and #9 fail and the
    rest pass; with the fix all pass.
-->
